From af76b500bffe98cb8e4114dc23b3106aae20b6e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:58:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GBM] Video at its own rate with VRR: off by default,
 where the display has no mode at the video's rate, or always

"Video at its own rate with VRR (no change of mode)" of the first builds of 1.1 was an Expert switch, off:
on, on any display with VRR, an SDR or HDR10 video (and HDR10+ on the RTX 40 and RTX 50 series) played
in the mode of the menus with VRR, the screen not going black when it started and stopped. The last
change made that same switch take only a display without a mode at the video's rate, on by default:
that took the first way from whoever wanted it on a TV with modes of 24 Hz, and turned VRR on in the
modes of the menus of some displays without being asked. Now it is one setting with three values
(videoscreen.hadesvrrvideomode, VRR_VIDEO::Mode), as Kodi's settings with more than two choices are:

- Off, the default: every mode set as in the builds before VRR video: no
  video at its own rate, and on NVIDIA HDMI VRR left off in every mode set while "HDMI variable refresh
  rate (VRR)" is off, the menus included (no VTEM "VRR on" there).
- Where the display has no mode at the video's rate: what the last change did, asked only after
  Kodi's whole choice of a mode (VRR_VIDEO::Automatic(), AutoForDisplay()).
- Always: what the first builds of 1.1 did with their switch on, asked before Kodi's choice
  (TakesBeforeKodi(), CResolutionUtils::ChooseBestResolution()), every mode set leaving HDMI VRR to the
  driver; with the check of the signal by the out-fences of the flips that the last change added, and
  where VRR does not come on the mode is chosen as without it.

CHdmiVrrOff::Allowed() and Media VRR in the mode sets of the menus follow VRR_VIDEO::VrrInModeSets()
of the value and the display (CWinSystemGbm::VrrVideoInModeSets()), no longer the boolean whatever
the display.

The boolean (videoscreen.hadesvrrvideo) stays, hidden, as the builds before read it, and is taken
over when the settings load: on (the "on" of the first builds of 1.1) is "Always", off or not saved is Off. The
rule is the one of the two settings of native Dolby Vision that took over booleans, now in
settings/SettingTakeOver.h for both (CDVEngineSettings::Migrate() calls it; nothing of what it does
changes), and CSettings takes over and follows every such pair in one list.

The help says what each value does, and that with VRR a TV or a monitor usually shows the refresh
rate of the mode in its own information (120 or 360 Hz) while the picture follows the video, with
where the makers' manuals say the real rate is shown (not checked); so does the VRR row of the player
information, shortly. In English and the three Spanish languages, with one new string (the value
"Where the display has no mode at the video's rate", core #62144, Estuary #54144); Off and Always are
Kodi's #351 and #20422.

Checked: the host tests (vrr_video_test.cpp: the values, VrrInModeSets() on the displays measured,
the take-over of the boolean; vrr_gui_test.cpp: with the setting off, every mode set of the G60SD and
the LG C5 asks for VRR off; with "where no mode" only the G60SD's leave it to the driver; with
"always" both), with their mutants; the changed files and the sources that include them compile with
the commands of the image's build. Not run on a GPU.
